# AF-EP-002 — Enterprise Information Ownership

**Project:** BTA V5.1 — HCGO Enterprise Persistence Architecture

**Status:** Approved

**Classification:** Analysis Finding

---

# Purpose

Identify the authoritative ownership of enterprise information across HCGO.

This analysis establishes authoritative enterprise information ownership prior to Enterprise Information Flow Analysis and Persistence Architecture.

This analysis identifies enterprise information ownership only.

It does not define runtime execution, implementation, persistence, APIs, database structures, or technology.

---

# Analysis Principles

Enterprise Information Ownership shall identify:

- Enterprise information categories
- Authoritative ownership
- Information stewardship
- Information responsibility
- Authorized consumers
- Authorized references

Enterprise Information Ownership shall not identify:

- Database tables
- Data structures
- Foreign keys
- Runtime information flow
- APIs
- Message formats
- Persistence implementation
- PostgreSQL schema

---

# Enterprise Ownership Principles

Every enterprise information category shall have one and only one authoritative enterprise owner.

Authoritative ownership shall be unique, explicit, and governed.

Ownership may only change through approved enterprise governance.

Information may have many authorized consumers.

Consumers may reference, classify, validate, or use enterprise information, but ownership never transfers through consumption.

Information ownership remains independent of implementation, persistence, and technology.

