# Analysis Summary

Enterprise information ownership is independent of implementation, persistence, runtime execution, and technology.

Every enterprise information category has one and only one authoritative owner.

Ownership establishes enterprise authority.

Consumers and references establish enterprise collaboration.

Ownership never transfers through consumption.

---

# Current Assessment

Enterprise Information Ownership establishes the authoritative ownership model for enterprise information across HCGO.

These ownership boundaries provide the foundation for:

- AF-EP-003 — Enterprise Information Flow
- Enterprise Conceptual Information Model
- Persistence Architecture
- Logical Data Modeling
- Future HCGO implementation

Enterprise information ownership intentionally precedes information flow to ensure that information movement always originates from an identified authoritative owner.